      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that basic police officer training includes an anti-stigma intervention and that training is argued to help officers interact adaptively and achieve good outcomes with people with mental illness, and that stigma/discrimination are a barrier to help-seeking. However, the definition adds that anti-stigma content reduces discriminatory attitudes that can affect “everyday life,” and the packet does not explicitly support the “everyday life” phrasing (it discusses burdens and factors like housing/work and help-seeking, but not “everyday life”)."
